.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt COMPRESS 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm compress
.Nd compress files with adaptive LZW (.Z)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl c
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl b Ar bits
.Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility compresses each
.Ar file
to
.Ar file Ns .Z
using the historical `.Z` LZW format
.Pq magic Ql 1f 9d .
The default maximum code width is 16 bits; block mode and clear codes are used.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c
Write the result to standard output and keep the input.
.It Fl d
Decompress instead of compress.
.It Fl b Ar bits
Use a maximum code width from 9 through 16.
.El
.Pp
On a file operation the input is removed after a successful write.
The target image requires a
file operand; standard input is not available.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A corrupt stream or I/O error exits with status 1; a usage error exits with status 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr uncompress 1 ,
.Xr zcat 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD implements the historical block-mode `.Z` LZW format.
